# Versioned releases

`main` is the integration trunk. Tags (`vX.Y.Z`) are frozen snapshots. Process: [docs/structured-releases.md](docs/structured-releases.md). When asked to cut a release, follow [.cursor/skills/cut-release/SKILL.md](../skills/cut-release/SKILL.md) (prepare changelog, version, and docs; do not commit or tag unless the user asks).

- Land user-visible work on `main` (short feature branches are fine). Unreleased bullets: [project-context.mdc](project-context.mdc).
- Do not bump `cleave.__version__`, add a dated `## [X.Y.Z]` section, tag, or GitHub Release unless asked to cut a release. `__version__` is last-shipped until a cut.
- Do not introduce a long-lived `develop` or `release/*` trunk, GitFlow, or holding features off `main`.

A `release/X.Y` branch is only for a freeze window or a patch of a shipped tag, and only when asked.
